WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:05.940
If you run sales enablement,
you know this moment.

2
00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:13.463
The sales plan for next year lands, and it
asks for more than last year: more hires,

3
00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:20.847
more launches, a kickoff, new talk
tracks. Your team did not get bigger.

4
00:00:21.333 --> 00:00:26.855
So the work slips. Programs ship
late. The kickoff gets no follow-up.

5
00:00:26.905 --> 00:00:34.177
Reps do not finish what you built.
The tools you pay for sit half-used.

6
00:00:34.227 --> 00:00:38.640
And your CRO sees completion
counts, not results.

7
00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:45.406
I started Enablement Works to
fix the hours, not the people.

8
00:00:45.456 --> 00:00:51.619
We are the production and operations
engine for enablement teams.

9
00:00:51.669 --> 00:00:55.200
You set the strategy. We do the work.

10
00:00:55.700 --> 00:01:02.575
We build the content, roleplays
and programs your roadmap needs,

11
00:01:02.625 --> 00:01:12.783
in your methodology and in the tools you
already own: microlearning, AI roleplays,

12
00:01:12.833 --> 00:01:18.753
launch kits, onboarding and certification.

13
00:01:18.803 --> 00:01:21.597
Your enablement lead approves every brief.

14
00:01:21.647 --> 00:01:26.963
A senior reviewer approves
every asset before you see it.

15
00:01:27.467 --> 00:01:30.325
Then we run the programs.

16
00:01:30.375 --> 00:01:36.595
We launch with a message from
your sales leader, nudge reps,

17
00:01:36.645 --> 00:01:45.229
send managers the list of who has not
started, and escalate when completion is low.

18
00:01:45.733 --> 00:01:52.556
Every month your CRO gets
one page: activity, practice,

19
00:01:52.606 --> 00:01:58.342
behavior where you record calls,
and outcomes from your CRM.

20
00:01:58.392 --> 00:02:01.413
Your enablement lead presents it.

21
00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:12.851
We start with a three-week Diagnostic.
It shows what your plan needs,

22
00:02:12.901 --> 00:02:18.719
what your team can deliver
and what your tools return,

23
00:02:18.769 --> 00:02:21.737
and it ends with a 12-month
roadmap and the first two programs.

24
00:02:22.233 --> 00:02:25.177
If you want to know your own numbers first,

25
00:02:25.227 --> 00:02:30.746
book a free 20-minute Capacity Check with
your CRO and your head of enablement.

26
00:02:30.796 --> 00:02:32.628
You keep the results.
